    "why": "rosie_1420_v1 reuses three of the 1400's castings verbatim: the link_2, link_3 and link_6 meshes have the same vertex set in both bundles, point for point, so a sphere fitted to one is fitted to the other and those coverage numbers carry over exactly. link_1, link_4 and link_5 are different parts (vertices move a median of 24.8, 25.4 and 5.3 mm), and the 1400's spheres left them blind by 79.0, 58.3 and 8.8 mm against the 10 mm that spheres.WORST_UNCOVERED_M calls out, so they were authored by hand. Measured 2026-09-12.",
    "link_4_refit": "link_4's first hand fit covered the forearm with four spheres over 100 mm and it made the ARM self-colliding at its own reset pose: the model put link_4 35.2 mm inside link_6 where the real castings are 43.9 mm apart, so every node the lattice found feasible was then rejected by the screen and no seam crossed at any placement. Refit 2026-09-12 -- the two spheres at the wrist end came down from 104.5 and 93.3 mm to 73.2 and 74.2 mm and one of 53.6 mm was added between them. Reset-pose clearance to link_6 is now +8.3 mm, over_coverage 1.4055 -> 1.0986, and worst_uncovered 0.96 -> 3.79 mm, which is under-cover the CCD verifier re-checks and in family with link_1's 4.44 and link_6's 3.27. On the bring-up request 4 of 11 seams cross and all four pass T2."
  },
